Aggregate.prompt:
Aggregate the prior reviewer round into ONE structured review payload for PR #${vars.pr_number}.

PRIOR ROUND OUTPUTS (one block per reviewer):
${Review.output}

Return STRICT JSON with no surrounding prose, no markdown fences, exactly:
{
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "<one-to-three sentence aggregate; lead with APPROVE or REQUEST CHANGES then the reasoning>",
  "action": "merge" | "request_changes"
}

Use action=merge ONLY when every reviewer line was APPROVE. Otherwise action=request_changes. event is always COMMENT (this demo runs single-user; Forgejo refuses APPROVED/REQUEST_CHANGES on own PRs). The downstream PostReview node reads `action` to decide whether to auto-merge: action=merge → POST /merge → fires pr-merged webhook → arc terminates clean. action=request_changes → no merge, the loop waits for the next pr-feedback signal.
